    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497">

                <pb facs="0419" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg407"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.24/53: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hibbard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-24T11:00:00-00:44">December 24,
                            1942—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:49 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram 312, December 4, 10 p.m. I have had a conversation with
                    President Barclay this morning for the first time in 3 weeks as he has been
                    confined to his bed. We discussed all pending matters which will be taken up in
                    individual telegrams.</p>
                <p>The Liberian Government is still desirous of receiving lend-lease aid and
                    accordingly requests that the President’s certification of Liberia’s eligibility
                    be made public<anchor n="53" xml:id="d497-f1"/> in the usual way and that the
                    Department proceed with the preparation of a lend-lease agreement between the
                    two countries.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hibbard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d497-f1" n="53" xml:id="d497-f1-content">
                <p>For the public statement regarding Lend-Lease aid to Liberia, see Department of
                    State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, January 16, 1943, p. 59.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
